# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provokes the enemies you picked onto each other, two at a time, while any is free.
# Every enemy you pick joins a pool. Each round, the first two in the pool that are not
# your current target and whose labels show neither provoked nor a barding break are
# provoked onto each other, a lone one onto your current target. Nothing remembers who
# was paired with whom: the label is the state, so a pair that ran out or lost one side
# to death is paired again from whatever is free, with no limit on the number of pairs.
# The spells and the other bard skills stay on your current target. There is no search
# for enemies you never picked: Razor has no expression that finds an enemy, and the
# Next Monster Target hotkeys move lastharmful, which fight/target takes for a pick.
# Leave the block out of the recipe to stop provoking.
#
# @ hotkeys Cancel Current Target
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ wait
#
#   interval__provo_seen
#      How often the pool is looked over while pairs are being made, the same two
#      seconds bard/peace reads its labels on.
#
#   interval__provo_retry
#      How long the next round waits after one that found nothing to provoke, or could
#      not reach its pair. A new pick cuts it short. A plain failure needs no wait of its
#      own: "fail to incite anger" starts the 5 second peace/provo bar (cooldowns.xml).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! interval__provo_seen 2000
@setvar! interval__provo_retry 5000


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ timer
#
#   timer__provo_seen, timer__provo_retry
#      Ready on the first pass.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
timer__provo_seen interval__provo_seen
timer__provo_retry interval__provo_retry


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ state
#
#   var__provo_first, var__provo_second
#      Scratch: the two enemies found free this round, provoked first onto second. 0 when
#      not found.
#
#   var__provo_skip
#      An enemy left out of the next round because the last provocation could not reach
#      it, or got an answer this block does not know, so another pair gets the try.
#
#   var__provo_dropped
#      Scratch: 1 when the round found an enemy dead or gone, so the pool is rebuilt.
#
#   var__provo_answer
#      Scratch: what the server answered, 0 nothing known, 1 provoked, 2 failed, 3 out of
#      reach, 4 the first one cannot be provoked, 5 the slot was not free yet.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@setvar! var__provo_first 0
@setvar! var__provo_second 0
@setvar! var__provo_skip 0
@setvar! var__provo_dropped 0
@setvar! var__provo_answer 0


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ setup
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pool is kept across Plays, so a loop that recycle restarts still knows the fight.
# Dead and far ones leave on the next round. The enemies that refused a provocation
# outright get a new chance on every Play, in case the refusal was a passing one.
if not listexists 'list__provo_known'
    createlist 'list__provo_known'
endif
if not listexists 'list__provo_keep'
    createlist 'list__provo_keep'
endif
removelist 'list__provo_never'
createlist 'list__provo_never'


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @ loop
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # PROVOKE
    #
    # Runs on every pass, outside the fight group, so every pick joins the pool even when
    # it is still out of reach. A new pick also cuts the wait short, so it is provoked
    # within a pass. An enemy that died, or left config__acquire_range, is dropped from
    # the pool on the next round.
    #
    # Pairs follow the pool order, which is the order the enemies were first picked. The
    # current target is skipped in that walk and only takes a lone free one: two free
    # enemies away from it fight each other while it keeps its Peace. With three, A and B
    # provoked and C your target, A and B are provoked again when it runs out and C stays
    # pacified. A pacified creature can still be provoked (Bard Necro 02.P).
    #
    # Peace and Provocation share one server slot (Bard Necro part 2), so this goes
    # before bard/peace and bard/disco in the pass and takes the slot, and Music, whenever
    # a pair is free. Peace and Provocation both last 51 seconds here (Bard Necro 01.D),
    # so a pair or the Peace takes the slot about once a minute. bard/peace leaves a
    # provoked target alone, and Ensemble still counts it: its condition is Discord and
    # Peace or Provocation.
    #
    # The first enemy is targeted, then the second, and each goes into var__target_hold
    # just before: the last one targeted is not always the current target, and a refused
    # first target leaves lastharmful on that one, so no block takes either for a pick.
    # The Journal lines this reads are read off first, so a line left over from a cast
    # cannot pass for this answer. The answers are the lines other Outlands bard scripts
    # read, and "fail to incite anger" is the one cooldowns.xml and the profile key on.
    # ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    if var__combat_target != 0 and not inlist 'list__provo_known' var__combat_target
        pushlist 'list__provo_known' var__combat_target
        settimer "timer__provo_seen" interval__provo_seen
        settimer "timer__provo_retry" interval__provo_retry
    endif

    if var__fighting = 1 and timer "timer__provo_seen" >= interval__provo_seen and timer "timer__provo_retry" >= interval__provo_retry and cooldown "peace/provo" = 0 and cooldown "music" = 0 and skill "Provocation" > 0 and not warmode and var__instrument_ok = 1 and var__my_instrument != 0 and not targetexists and not casting
        settimer "timer__provo_seen" 0
        @setvar! var__provo_first 0
        @setvar! var__provo_second 0
        @setvar! var__provo_dropped 0
        clearlist 'list__provo_keep'

        foreach provo_mob in list__provo_known
            if find provo_mob ground -1 -1 config__acquire_range as alias__provo_mob
                if dead alias__provo_mob
                    @setvar! var__provo_dropped 1
                else
                    pushlist 'list__provo_keep' provo_mob

                    if var__provo_second = 0 and provo_mob != var__combat_target and provo_mob != var__provo_skip
                        if not inlist 'list__provo_never' provo_mob
                            if find provo_mob ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__provo_near
                                getlabel alias__provo_near label__provo_mob

                                if "provoked" in label__provo_mob or "barding break" in label__provo_mob
                                    # Busy, or cannot take one now.
                                elseif var__provo_first = 0
                                    @setvar! var__provo_first provo_mob
                                else
                                    @setvar! var__provo_second provo_mob
                                endif
                            endif
                        endif
                    endif
                endif
            else
                @setvar! var__provo_dropped 1
            endif
        endfor

        if var__provo_dropped = 1
            clearlist 'list__provo_known'
            foreach provo_mob in list__provo_keep
                pushlist 'list__provo_known' provo_mob
            endfor
        endif

        @setvar! var__provo_skip 0

        # A lone free enemy goes onto the current target, if that one can take it.
        if var__provo_first != 0 and var__provo_second = 0
            if not inlist 'list__provo_never' var__combat_target
                if find var__combat_target ground -1 -1 config__target_range as alias__provo_target
                    getlabel alias__provo_target label__provo_target

                    if "provoked" in label__provo_target or "barding break" in label__provo_target
                        # Taken too. The lone one waits for the next free enemy.
                    else
                        @setvar! var__provo_second var__combat_target
                    endif
                endif
            endif
        endif

        if var__provo_second = 0
            # Nothing to provoke: look again in five seconds, or at the next pick.
            settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
        else
            if insysmsg "play successfully, provoking"
                # Read off, with the three below, before this round's answer.
            endif
            if insysmsg "too far away"
                # Read off.
            endif
            if insysmsg "Target cannot be seen"
                # Read off.
            endif
            if insysmsg "You must wait a few moments"
                # Read off.
            endif

            useskill 'Provocation'
            waitfortarget wait__bard_target

            # Answered once, the way bard/peace does.
            if insysmsg "What instrument shall you play"
                target var__my_instrument
                waitfortarget wait__bard_target

                if insysmsg "That is not a musical instrument"
                    @setvar! var__my_instrument 0
                endif
            endif

            if targetexists
                @setvar! var__target_hold var__provo_first
                target var__provo_first
                waitfortarget wait__bard_target
            endif

            if targetexists
                @setvar! var__target_hold var__provo_second
                target var__provo_second
                wait wait__short
            endif

            if targetexists
                hotkey "Cancel Current Target"
                wait wait__short
            endif

            # The answer comes within a second. Read on every round until it does, with
            # no break: this loop sits inside the main one.
            @setvar! var__provo_answer 0
            for 5
                if var__provo_answer = 0
                    if insysmsg "play successfully, provoking"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 1
                    elseif insysmsg "fail to incite anger"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 2
                    elseif insysmsg "too far away" or insysmsg "Target cannot be seen"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 3
                    elseif insysmsg "incite that"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 4
                    elseif insysmsg "You must wait a few moments"
                        @setvar! var__provo_answer 5
                    else
                        wait wait__short
                    endif
                endif
            endfor

            # Provoked and failed are both held by the peace/provo bar. The rest wait, and
            # an answer this block does not know, or none, leaves the first one out next
            # time, so one refusal cannot hold every round.
            if var__provo_answer = 4
                pushlist 'list__provo_never' var__provo_first
                overhead "[ provo, wrong ]" 1288 var__provo_first
            elseif var__provo_answer = 5
                settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
            elseif var__provo_answer = 3 or var__provo_answer = 0
                @setvar! var__provo_skip var__provo_first
                settimer "timer__provo_retry" 0
            endif
        endif
    endif
